[ti:Holy Shade]
[ar:EdgarAllanMusic]
[al:Sidd-hartha.text - Reawakened]

[00:02.66]Yeah... shade gettin' cold... river callin' my name
[00:20.25](Ommm...)
[00:21.89]Grew up in the shade of the house by the boats on the bank
[00:25.09]Sun brownin' my shoulders while the holy waters sank
[00:28.03]Ablutions every morning, verses from the old
[00:30.50]But the vessel stayed empty, quiet hunger took hold
[00:33.66]Father pourin' wisdom like honey in my ears
[00:36.19]Mother's grace like gold, still the soul stayed uncontrolled
[00:39.57]Dreams flowin' from the stars at night
[00:42.29]Thoughts driftin' from the smoke of the rites
[00:44.54]Govinda at my side like a shadow on the wall
[00:47.00]Swore he'd follow me through fire if I answered the call
[00:50.21]Brahmins sang my praises, said the boy was gonna shine
[00:52.79]Every elder had a blessing, not a single word was mine
[00:55.81]Atman in the chest, they could name it, couldn't show it
[00:58.22]Had the whole map of heaven, never walked it, never knew it
[01:01.10]The path they laid was perfect... but it wasn't mine to write
[01:05.33]The arrow leaves the bow (the arrow leaves the bow)
[01:09.05]Om is the bow and the target is the soul
[01:13.10]The arrow leaves the bow (the arrow leaves the bow)
[01:15.12]Shade gettin' cold, now it's time for me to go
[01:17.53]Told my father in the night I'd be leavin' with the dawn
[01:20.35]He said no, I didn't move, stood in silence till he's gone
[01:23.52]Moonlight through the window, feet planted on the floor
[01:25.86]Stood there through the darkness while he paced behind the door
[01:28.70]Every hour he came back and I was still standin' there
[01:31.49]Legs shakin', heart steady, eyes locked on the air
[01:34.25]By the mornin' he could see I was already gone
[01:36.88]"Find the bliss in the forest, come back and pass it on"
[01:39.79]Bare feet on the dust, old life fadin' in the rearview
[01:42.85]No more sacred songs, no more rituals to lean to
[01:45.74]Every step a question, every breath a silent war
[01:48.04]Between what they taught me... and what I'm searchin' for
[01:50.84]Fig trees still wavin', river still callin' my name
[01:53.54]But the voice inside louder, rewritin' the game
[01:56.48]No more borrowed light, no more secondhand flame
[01:59.14]Just the road, just the unknown, just the hunger for my own name
[02:02.71]The arrow leaves the bow (the arrow leaves the bow)
[02:05.37]Om is the bow and the target is the soul
[02:08.22]The arrow leaves the bow (the arrow leaves the bow)
[02:10.82]Shade gettin' cold, now it's time for me to go
[02:13.34]The arrow leaves the bow... no more followin' the line
[02:17.86]Gotta find the target deep inside this mind of mine
[02:23.47]Left the sacred grove, left the holy name behind
[02:29.09]Searchin' for the Self no teacher's word could find
[02:34.78]Om in the chest, every heartbeat is a drum
[02:38.12]Every prayer I ever learned turned to echo, turned to hum
[02:40.92]Not runnin' from the temple, I'm the temple on the road
[02:43.68]Carry nothin' but the question, and the question is the load
[02:46.48]Three gaunt men at the edge of the town, ash on the skin
[02:49.30]Samanas passin' by and I'm already in
[02:52.10]Govinda caught my sleeve, said "brother, where you go, I go"
[02:54.76]Shaved the old life off, left it in the dust below
[02:57.53]Gave my robes to the beggars, gave my name to the wind
[03:00.36]Every comfort that I owned was a chain around my skin
[03:03.32]Hunger as a teacher, the sun as a whip
[03:05.85]Learned to stand without a shadow, learned to breathe without a grip
[03:08.75]The house by the river fadin' small behind the trees
[03:11.38]Mother's voice, father's silence, carried off on the breeze
[03:14.67]The shade was holy, but the shade was a cage
[03:16.86]Now the arrow's in the air and I'm writin' my own page
[03:20.47]The arrow leaves the bow (the arrow leaves the bow)
[03:22.96]Om is the bow and the target is the soul
[03:26.02]The arrow leaves the bow (the arrow leaves the bow)
